    "result_text": "The full build passes \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both tests are green. The build also compiles the entire project (OpenAPI DTO generation, MapStruct mapper, all OfficeFloor function classes).\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented soft-delete for owners across the entity, persistence, endpoints, and API schema:\n\n1. **`Owner` entity** (`model/Owner.java`) \u2014 added a persisted `boolean deleted` field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`), defaulting to `false`, with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`.\n\n2. **`DeleteOwner`** (`rest/function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`) \u2014 `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` now sets `deleted = true` and `save`s the owner instead of removing the row, so the record is retained and the endpoint still returns 2xx (204 via the unchanged `RespondWithNoContent`).\n\n3. **`EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity`** (`rest/function/owner/EnsureUniqueOwnerIdentity.java`) \u2014 the create endpoint's duplicate/identity (household) check now skips owners flagged `deleted`, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was soft-deleted.\n\n4. **OpenAPI spec** (`openapi.yml`) \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` schema, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it (the MapStruct mapper maps it automatically by name). A newly created owner reads back `deleted: false`.\n\n5. **Schemas** (`db/{h2,hsqldb,mysql,postgres}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` to the `owners` table (DEFAULT-before-NOT NULL ordering required by HSQLDB, which the test profile uses). `findById` intentionally does not filter deleted, so a soft-deleted owner is still fetchable.\n\nBoth spec tests pass: `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` (create \u2192 `deleted:false`, delete \u2192 still 200 with `deleted:true`) and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` (re-creating an identical owner after soft-delete succeeds).",
